# Copy to .env and edit. docker compose reads it automatically.
# Cipherfilm needs HTTPS in front: any reverse proxy, pointed at http://127.0.0.1:8080 (docs/SELF-HOSTING.md).

# Required: the name(s) your proxy serves, comma-separated. Requests for any other name are refused.
PUBLIC_HOSTS=photos.example.com

# 1: exactly one proxy in front that adds X-Forwarded-For. 0: a chain of proxies, a Cloudflare Tunnel or Tailscale Serve.
#TRUST_PROXY=1
# Proxies whose X-Forwarded-For is believed (addresses or CIDRs, comma-separated). Empty: loopback and private networks.
#TRUSTED_PROXIES=
# The port on 127.0.0.1 your proxy connects to.
#APP_PORT=8080
# The address it listens on. 127.0.0.1: only a proxy on this host. A proxy in a Docker container: the Docker bridge's
# address (often 172.17.0.1). Never 0.0.0.0 on a machine reachable from the internet: that serves plain HTTP to everyone.
#APP_BIND=127.0.0.1

# --- Optional ---
# Passkeys from the Android app: the signing certificates (SHA-256) and packages allowed, also served in
# /.well-known/assetlinks.json. Default: the official app. Add a self-built app's key; "none" for no app.
#ANDROID_APP_CERTS=87:D9:E9:AB:85:5B:03:E7:D7:D3:15:2F:5A:76:A4:D8:AF:B5:D3:8E:FC:A3:B9:93:2A:D9:3F:1B:A1:7C:67:12
#ANDROID_APP_PACKAGES=app.cipherfilm
# The image. Default: the released one, following every 2.x release. Pin one version with :X.Y.Z, or use your own build.
#CIPHERFILM_IMAGE=ghcr.io/basmatiactivist/cipherfilm:2
# Name of the Docker volume that holds the database and the encrypted files.
#DATA_VOLUME=cipherfilm_data
